FASTAPI
*FastAPI is a modern Python web framework, very efficient in building APIs. It is based on Pythons type hints feature that has been added since Python 3.6 onwards.
*It supports asynchronous programming and automatically generates OpenAPI documentation.

UVICORN
*Uvicorn is an ASGI server used to run FastAPI applications.
   uvicorn main:app --reload
*--reload   automatically reloads during development


HTTP Methods

| Method | Purpose                |
| ------ | ---------------------- |
| GET    | Retrieve data          |
| POST   | Create data            |
| PUT    | Update entire resource |
| PATCH  | Partially update       |
| DELETE | Delete data            |


HTTP STATUS CODES

200 → OK
201 → Created
204 → No Content
400 → Bad Request
401 → Unauthorized
403 → Forbidden
404 → Not Found
422 → Validation Error
500 → Internal Server Error

REQUEST BODY
*Data sent from the client to the server is called the request body.
@app.post("/students")
def create_student(student: Student):
    return student

DIFFERENCE BETWEEN PUT AND PATCH
*PUT is generally used to completely update or replace a resource, whereas PATCH is used to partially update a resource. 
For example, if I want to update all details of a student, I can use PUT. If I only want to change the student's age, I can use PATCH

